<ol>
<li>youth to click one of the provided emotions based on how they’re feeling</li>
<li>a scripture to popup associated with the emotion they selected</li>
</ol>

<p>I’m new to coding (have only been doing it for a few weeks outside of work) and I’m stumped as to where I’ve gone wrong.</p>

<p>Originally I was using a hover feature, but now I want to upgrade to a popup as mentioned in bullet 2.</p>

<p>Here’s my codepen: <a href="https://codepen.io/mj2913/pen/pXgxOz" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codepen.io/mj2913/pen/pXgxOz</a></p>

<pre><code>    &lt;div class="happy-thumb popup" onclick="myFunction()"&gt;
        &lt;p&gt;happy
          &lt;span class="popup-thumb-span" id="happyPopup"&gt;I praise you, for I am fearfully and wonderfully made. Wonderful are your works; my soul knows it very well. Psalm 139:14&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<pre><code>    &lt;script&gt;
