            if (mDrawerLayout.isDrawerOpen(mDrawerList)) {
                mDrawerLayout.closeDrawer(mDrawerList);
            } else {
                mDrawerLayout.openDrawer(mDrawerList);
            }
        }
    });

    // Add your custom toolbar to your content layout
    content_layout.addView(customToolbar);

    // ... [rest of your setup code]
}
```

3. **Update Your `ActionBarDrawerToggle` Setup**:

When using a custom view, you may not necessarily need the `ActionBarDrawerToggle` unless you want to sync the state. In most cases, the manual approach provides immediate feedback without implicit toggling states assuming the visual part is managed completely by the view you created.

In the case where you still want the toggle function, create it without the need to show the icon in the toolbar, relying on your custom click listener for the ImageView.

