Once the data is set in the ViewModel, you can observe it in the `CoursesFragment` to get updates whenever the selected type changes.

### Conclusion

By using either callbacks or shared ViewModels, you can move away from relying on `setTargetFragment`, which can lead to the type of errors you encountered. This not only resolves the error but also promotes better decoupling between your fragments. If you still want to use `FragmentManager`, make sure that both the `Fragment` and `DialogFragment` are instantiated and managed by the same `FragmentManager`.

